Unwine reuses work from these projects, each under its own licence:
- NotProton (GPL-3.0): the ntdll detour sources in tools/steamplay/ntdll-patch, from which
  Sources/Unwine/SteamPlay/NtdllRecipes.swift is generated; Unwine downloads NotProton's
  release payload (Steam add-on, lsteamclient, steam.exe shim) at setup time.
- Wine (LGPL-2.1+), packaged by Gcenx as Sikarugir engines; downloaded at setup time.
- Sikarugir Template runtime (GStreamer LGPL, MoltenVK Apache-2.0, DXMT, DXVK zlib, KosmicKrisp MIT);
  downloaded at setup time. Apple's D3DMetal inside it is never extracted. On this Mac, Unwine makes
  patched copies of DXVK's d3d9.dll, the KosmicKrisp driver and Wine's ntdll.dll; the downloaded
  originals are not changed.
- Apple D3DMetal (Game Porting Toolkit): imported only from the user's own download from Apple.
- Valve's Steam client files: downloaded from Valve at setup time.
- Highball game database (gethighball.com): curated data CC0-1.0; its anti-cheat fields come from
  AreWeAntiCheatYet (MIT). Unwine downloads the whole list and keeps it on this Mac only.
- Windows Steam client for Online mode: Valve's own installer, downloaded from Valve when the user
  sets up Online mode.
- x87sidecar (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Lifeisawful, later work by athei; github.com/athei/x87sidecar):
  the release build x87sidecar_entitled, downloaded from its GitHub release only when the user turns
  on Faster x87 math for a game. Unwine checks its SHA-256 and does not change the program.
